From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: back micro-cuts from #1586, the back side (EDEN_UP_BACKX=1, off unless set)

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii 5e428570d2 (PR #1586, Zortos (zortos293) with capy-ai), its "skip back
locks and gathers that change nothing" part, itself from jpkto/Lichii 7a5e5357cb and f5edeabdbb
(the EDEN_NX2_BACKX_* switches). The page split of the same PR is our 0835; the draw side is 1005.

EDEN_UP_BACKX=1 (exact "1"):
- GPU::InvalidateGPUCache (~900 calls a frame) gathers only when a core's dirty memory manager shows
  a write (GPUDirtyMemoryManager::MayHavePending: `current` has bits). A write collected after the
  check is gathered by the next call, as one collected just after a gather is. Ours adds guards
  the upstream base lacks: only with the page split on (0835; without it a crossing write can leave
  `current` empty while back_buffer holds one), not with EDEN_UP_HELD_VS_DOWNLOAD (its rounds
  release held pages), and with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD only while nothing gathered at a present, held
  or re-dirtied waits for a gather (one lock and two empty checks).
- AccelerateInlineToMemory (deferred inline path, Ampere) skips the buffer cache's lock when no
  written 4 KiB page is marked GPU-written (g_nx2_gpu_written_pages: both places that add to
  gpu_modified_ranges mark it, the bits never clear) or is a command list page. InlineMemory only
  uploads into gpu_modified_ranges and Nx2NoteListHostWrite only acts on list pages, so the locked
  section would change nothing.
- UsageTracker::Reset clears only the words Track set since the last reset (a 1 GiB buffer's
  tracker is 2 MiB of words, cleared every frame before).
- OnCacheInvalidations takes each cache's lock once for all the writes (texture, then buffer with
  ClaimCpuWrites first, then the shader cache) instead of twice per write.
EDEN_UP_BACKX_VERIFY=1 (with it, diagnostic): every skip also does the work it replaces; the gather
check counts collects to tell a raced write from a missed one; mismatches log
"EDEN_UP_BACKX verify mismatch" (64 at most) and count as "misses" (must stay 0).
Count line (HW_GPU, every 10 s, looked at every 4096 gathers): "EDEN_UP_BACKX in 10 s: gathers N
skipped N (kept by a guard N), inline writes N lock skips N, tracker resets N words cleared N spared
N, invalidation batches N writes N | draw: ... | verify races N misses N".
Switches read in VideoCore::CreateGPU (after env.txt). Unset: as before.
Files: core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h, video_core/gpu.cpp, video_core.cpp, up_backx.h (new),
buffer_cache/usage_tracker.h, renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp. No translation id input: KEEPS
THE STORE.

---
