+    /// EDEN_UP_BACKX (zortos293/Lichii #1586, from jpkto 7a5e5357cb): false when Gather would
+    /// find nothing. With the page split every Collect that adds a write leaves its transform,
+    /// with bits, in `current` (by compare-exchange, or by exchange after pushing the one before
+    /// to back_buffer under `guard`), and only Gather, which takes back_buffer too, empties
+    /// `current` again. Without the locks: a Collect it misses is one the caller may order after
+    /// itself. Without the split a crossing write can leave `current` with no bits while
+    /// back_buffer holds a write, so callers ask this only with SplitAtPages().
